# Prioritize local changes during merges
# This ensures local versions are kept when conflicts occur with Overleaf
*.tex merge=ours
*.bib merge=ours
*.png merge=ours
*.jpg merge=ours
*.pdf merge=ours
# Text files - prefer local
*.md merge=ours
*.txt merge=ours
# forthcoming binary tool for live conversion of math expressions in terminal
laterm/* filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
data/pantheon_plus/*.cov filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
# The rulings docket is an append-only ledger: concurrent branches always append
# at the tail, which vanilla merge flags as a conflict. union keeps both sides —
# exactly the ledger's semantics. (Ordering of concurrent blocks may vary; each
# block is dated, so chronology is recoverable. 2026-07-19, after 5 manual
# both-kept-main-first resolutions of this exact conflict class.)
_orchestration/2026-07-10_rulings-docket.md merge=union
# Extension 2026-07-19: the meter charter and the Regime-IV audit doc are the
# other two recurrent append-only collision targets (amendments/addenda at the
# tail from concurrent lanes). Same union semantics as the docket.
research/2026-07-16_f6-bath-meter_CHARTER.md merge=union
research/2026-07-17_regime-iv-dissipation-audit.md merge=union
